# Rows to merge into docs/TECH-DEBT.md

Source: Phase 1 for `play/src/front/Stores/MediaStore.ts` (2026-11-12). Baseline `HEAD` = `fdd651abf`, `MediaStore.ts` sha256 `c224e56f…5329460908c4`. Evidence: `docs/audits/tech-debt/phase1-mediastore/README.md`. Line numbers are `HEAD`'s.

## Debt Ledger rows

| Item | Location | Type | Risk | Effort | Priority | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| MD-01: when `getUserMedia` fails with `OverconstrainedError` on `deviceId`, both chosen devices are reset: `requestedCameraDeviceIdStore` and `requestedMicrophoneDeviceIdStore` become `undefined`. A camera that can no longer be opened also drops a microphone that works, and the next request uses the default microphone. The preferred device stays in `localStorage`, so only the next device-list event (`deviceListStore`'s subscription) restores it. | `MediaStore.ts:952-965` | quirk (the error does not say which track failed, so both are reset) | low to medium. A user with a headset and a stale camera choice talks into the laptop microphone until a device is plugged or unplugged. | S (retry the kinds one at a time, or reset only the kind whose request fails alone) | P3 | pinned ("MD-01 (pinned): a chosen camera the browser cannot open also drops the chosen microphone"); no fix in this phase |
| MD-02: a constraint change that arrives while `getUserMedia` is pending makes the pending result stale. When it resolves, every track it opened is stopped (`:912-917`), and the next run asks again, including for the devices it still wants. Two store changes in the same tick outside `batchGetUserMediaStore` open the camera twice: the first stream is thrown away. A camera toggle during the room's batched request opens the microphone twice. | `MediaStore.ts:912-917`, `:1033-1054` | performance (weak devices) | medium. Each open costs 0.3 to 3 s and device start-up work (the module's own comment at `:520-524`). Real requests take that long, so the window is wide in a browser; the fakes resolve at once. Not measured in a browser. | M (keep the tracks of a stale result that the newer constraints still want, or coalesce changes before the first request) | P2 | pinned (two tests: "MD-02 (pinned): without the batch, …" and "MD-02 (pinned): a change during a pending request, …"); open |
| MD-03: the access issue a failed request records is erased by the retry that the same failure triggers. The camera branch calls `requestedCameraState.disableWebcam()`, which queues a new run, then sets `cameraAccessIssueStore`. The queued run starts with `cameraAccessIssueStore.set(null)` and `microphoneAccessIssueStore.set(null)`, so both stores are `null` again before anything renders. The microphone branch has the same order. `cameraButtonHelpContextStore` and `microphoneButtonHelpContextStore` therefore never return `"permission"` after a denial, and the action-bar tooltip (`CameraMenuItem.svelte`, `MicrophoneMenuItem.svelte`) never says that permission is the cause. `MediaSettingsPanel.svelte` still shows a denial when the Permissions API reports `"denied"`. | `MediaStore.ts:814-815`, `:978-979`, `:991-992`; `:1584-1625` | bug (refactor regression: state written, then erased by its own side effect) | medium (user-facing hint lost). The tooltip impact is inferred from the code; the test pins the store values. | S (clear an issue only in a run that requests that kind, plus when a device of that kind appears) | P2 | fixed by `fix-MD-03.patch` (a run clears the issue of a device only when it requests that device), which restores the behavior of `7d80fda06` that the refactor `02b30fa37` removed; pinned in `characterization-tests.patch`, test flipped. The help shows "permission" again after a denial, a state users have not seen since 2026-04-03: worth a look by the product owner |
| MD-04: `deviceListStore`'s `queryDeviceList` rethrows in its `.catch`, and nothing handles the rejection. Each failed `enumerateDevices()` becomes an unhandled promise rejection. | `MediaStore.ts:1539-1549` | bug (minor) | low (console and Sentry noise when device listing fails) | XS (drop the `throw`) | P3 | open; not pinned (inferred from the code) |
| MD-05: the comment at `:1505-1511` says nothing may watch the `getUserMedia` chain from module scope, but three module-scope subscriptions already do: `speakerListStore.subscribe` (`:1651`) and `deviceListStore.subscribe` (`:1669`) start `deviceListStore`, which subscribes `localStreamStore`, and `localStreamStore.subscribe` (`:1743`) does directly. The chain runs from import. No device is requested at import only because `myCameraStore` and `myMicrophoneStore` start `false`. | `MediaStore.ts:1505-1529`, `:1651`, `:1669`, `:1743` | design / doc drift | low today. Any store that starts `true` among the inputs of `mediaStreamConstraintsStore` would request a device at import. | S | P3 | partly pinned: test 1 asserts that loading the module asks the browser for nothing |
| MD-06: the module keeps its state in about 15 module-level `let`s (`currentStream`, `oldConstraints`, `warmAudio`, the three generation counters and queues, `previousComputed*`, the background pipe) and five module-scope subscriptions, with no reset. A test can only get a fresh state with `vi.resetModules()` and a new import, and the earlier copies stay subscribed to `window` focus events and keep reacting. | `MediaStore.ts:482-514`, `:645-691`, `:733-734`, `:1076-1077`, `:1148-1149`, `:1464-1466`, `:1665` | test debt / hidden global | low (production loads the module once) | M (move the stream pipeline into a class created once by the app, which tests can create per case) | P3 | open; the test file works around it in `afterEach` |
| MD-07: importing `MediaStore` first in a fresh module graph fails with `derived() expects stores as input, got a falsy value` at `ScreenSharingStore.ts:102`. `MediaStore` reaches the Phaser game through `IsStreamingStore` → `OnboardingStore` → `GameManager`, and from there `GameScene` → `MegaphoneStore` → `ScreenSharingStore`, which reads `MediaStore`'s exports before `MediaStore` has finished loading. The application's own load order hides it. | `IsStreamingStore.ts:5`, `OnboardingStore.ts:2`, `MegaphoneStore.ts:4-5`, `ScreenSharingStore.ts:15`, `:102` | design / import cycle | low in production (load order) and high for tests and tree-shaking: every test of `MediaStore` must mock `GameManager` or every module on the cycle. The middle of the chain is inferred from the imports; the `GameManager` mock removes the failure (`probe2` against `probe3`). | M (make `OnboardingStore` reach the scene through a store instead of `gameManager`, or move the onboarding check out of `IsStreamingStore`) | P2 | open; worked around by a link seam in the test file |
| MD-08: the `stop()` of `userMoved5SecondsAgoStore` and of `deviceChanged10SecondsAgoStore` does not clear the pending timeout, unlike `enabledWebCam10secondsAgoStore`'s. | `MediaStore.ts:210-212`, `:243-246` | quirk | low (singletons kept subscribed by `cameraEnergySavingStore`) | XS | P3 | open; not pinned |

